---
description: Signal code may read only a Causal view, where available_ts is at or before the decision time.
globs: "crates/signals/**/*.rs"
alwaysApply: false
---

# No lookahead

A signal function takes `parangsae_core::Causal<T>`. It does not take a raw slice, an `Observation`, or a bool that skips the gate.

`Causal` is built only by `Observation::causal_at`. Do not add a second constructor. The comparison is `available_ts <= decision`. `event_ts` and `received_ts` do not decide visibility.

A producer calls `Observation::new`. The decision clock is `DecisionTime::from_micros`.

A new signal entry point needs a proptest that mutates rows with `available_ts` after the decision and shows the output unchanged. Do not weaken the proptest in `crates/core/src/causal.rs` to fit a signal.
